@*
    Newsletters.razor
    Purpose: Public newsletter archive — subscribe card plus every past issue,
    newest send first, with paging.

    REQ-UI-053 (BRD-100) — only SENT, public, slugged issues are listed; each links to
    its own issue page at /newsletter/{slug}. Subscribing creates a PENDING subscriber
    until the mailed confirmation link is clicked (BRD-98).

    Dependencies: INewsletterService (published archive queries, REQ-FN-050),
                  ISubscriberRepo (confirmed-subscriber count),
                  NewsletterSubscribeCard, BlogBreadcrumb, BlogPagination.
    Layout: FullWidthLayout — content-focused, no blog sidebar (matches mockup 42).
    Mockup: docs/mockups/42-newsletter-archive.html
*@

@page "/newsletters"
@layout FullWidthLayout

<SiteBrandTitle Page="Newsletter — past issues" Separator=" · " />

@* UAT-027: was an inert `max-w-[900px]` (arbitrary-value utility, never applied — this
   build has no Tailwind JIT). This is a card-grid listing page, not article prose, so it
   is LAYOUT-tier content: it takes no extra cap and simply fills FullWidthLayout's
   `.site-container` (fluid, caps 1600px). *@
<div data-testid="newsletter-archive">

    <BlogBreadcrumb Items="@breadcrumbItems" />

    @* ---- Page header ---------------------------------------------------- *@
    <header class="mb-6 mt-6 flex flex-col gap-2">
        @* [REQ-UI-060] 2026-08-11 — back on TypographyH1. This was a plain <h1> with the
           component's own token classes copied onto it because 2.0.1's Typography* declared no
           CaptureUnmatchedValues, so the test hook had nowhere to live (TR-021), and because
           its font size was baked in with no way to override it (TR-020). Both are fixed:
           Typography* splats, and `Size` REPLACES the component's own size classes — including
           the responsive text-4xl lg:text-5xl step — which is why the size is passed as `Size`
           and not through `Class`. *@
        <TypographyH1 Size="TypographySize.Xl4"
                      Class="text-balance tracking-tight text-foreground"
                      data-testid="newsletter-archive-title">Newsletter</TypographyH1>
        @* UAT-027: was an inert `max-w-[40rem]` arbitrary-value utility (never applied — no
           Tailwind JIT in this build). `max-w-2xl` (672px) is a real, standard Tailwind
           utility (shipped in the prebuilt bundle) that keeps this one-line intro from
           stretching edge-to-edge now the page above it is fluid up to 1600px. *@
        <p class="max-w-2xl text-muted-foreground" data-testid="newsletter-archive-intro">
            A monthly note on .NET, Blazor and things I have been building.
            No spam, unsubscribe any time.
        </p>
    </header>

    @* ---- Subscribe (double opt-in + self-hosted captcha) ------------------ *@
    <div class="mb-8">
        <NewsletterSubscribeCard ConfirmedSubscriberCount="@confirmedSubscriberCount"
                                 TestId="newsletter-subscribe" />
    </div>

    <Separator />

    @* ---- Past issues ------------------------------------------------------ *@
    <section class="mt-8" aria-label="Past issues">
        <TypographyH2 Size="TypographySize.Xl"
                      Class="mb-4 tracking-tight text-foreground"
                      data-testid="newsletter-issues-heading">Past issues</TypographyH2>

        @if (isLoading)
        {
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4" data-testid="newsletter-issues-loading">
                @for (var placeholder = 0; placeholder < 3; placeholder++)
                {
                    <Skeleton Class="h-32 w-full rounded-lg" />
                }
            </div>
        }
        else if (issues.Count == 0)
        {
            <Empty Title="No issues published yet"
                   Description="The first issue is being written. Subscribe above and it will land in your inbox."
                   Class="py-12"
                   data-testid="newsletter-issues-empty">
                <Icon><LucideIcon Name="mail" Size="48" /></Icon>
            </Empty>
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-4" data-testid="newsletter-issues-list">
                @foreach (var issue in issues)
                {
                    var issueNumber = GetIssueNumber(issue);
                    <Card data-testid="newsletter-issue-card">
                        <CardContent Class="flex flex-col gap-2 p-6">

                            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                                <Badge data-testid="newsletter-issue-number">Issue #@issueNumber</Badge>
                                <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2" data-testid="newsletter-issue-date">
                                    <LucideIcon Name="calendar" Size="16" />
                                    @FormatSentOn(issue)
                                </span>
                            </div>

                            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold leading-snug">
                                <a href="/newsletter/@issue.Slug"
                                   class="text-foreground no-underline hover:text-primary hover:underline"
                                   data-testid="newsletter-issue-title">@issue.Title</a>
                            </h3>

                            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="newsletter-issue-excerpt">
                                @GetExcerpt(issue)
                            </p>

                            <div>
                                <Button Href="@($"/newsletter/{issue.Slug}")"
                                        Variant="ButtonVariant.Link"
                                        Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                        Class="px-0"
                                        data-testid="newsletter-issue-read">
                                    Read issue
                                    <LucideIcon Name="arrow-right" Size="16" />
                                </Button>
                            </div>

                        </CardContent>
                    </Card>
                }
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8">
                <BlogPagination CurrentPage="@currentPage"
                                TotalPages="@totalPages"
                                OnPageChanged="GoToPageAsync" />
            </div>
        }
    </section>

</div>
